    {
      "short_id": "short275",
      "angle": "The system that flagged him compared first and last name only. Not birth dates, not middle initials, not social security numbers.",
      "avoids": "No claim about how many people were wrongly flagged; no assertion that the Court found the system unlawful - this is the dissent; no invented identifier.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "A jury had already punished the same failure once, six years earlier. Why did it keep happening?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The last line returns to the two fields the first line named.",
      "era": "United States, 2005-2021",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "The law requires a credit agency to follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Among other things, it requires a consumer reporting agency to follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy in the reports it prepares."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-FCRA"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "In 2005 a consumer sued. TransUnion had sold an OFAC credit report about her to a car dealership.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "In 2005, a consumer sued.",
            "TransUnion had sold an OFAC credit report about her to a car dealership."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-CORTEZ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "It flagged Sandra Jean Cortez, born in May 1944, as a match for Sandra Cortes Quintero, born in June 1971.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The report flagged her — Sandra Jean Cortez, born in May 1944 — as a match for a person on the OFAC list: Sandra Cortes Quintero, born in June 1971."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-CORTEZ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "Twenty-seven years apart.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "Twenty-seven years apart."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-CORTEZ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "A court called the failure to compare birth dates, when they are available, reprehensible.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "stressing that TransUnion's failure to, at the very least, compare birth dates when they are available, was reprehensible"
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-CORTEZ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "Years later a justice described the system. It was rather rudimentary.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The system TransUnion used to decide which individuals to flag, he wrote, was rather rudimentary."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-THOMAS"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "It compared only the consumer's first and last name with the names on the OFAC list.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "It compared only the consumer's first and last name with the names on the OFAC list."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-THOMAS"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "It did not compare birth dates, middle initials, social security numbers, or any other available identifier.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "It did not compare birth dates, middle initials, social security numbers, or any other available identifier routinely used to collect and verify credit-report data."
          ],
          "claims": [
            "R-THOMAS"
          ]
        }
      ],
